  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "56f52da5a41d3f011783899e724de47a3df8f0e2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/56f52da5a41d3f011783899e724de47a3df8f0e2",
      "message": "Deploy the watcher image from the install step's pnpm store\n\nAs in the node image: without the store, deploy re-prepares the git-hosted\nmerkle-patricia-forestry package and fails for want of its dev tooling.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T08:45:39Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "355b58689c55ca969ce195edd651967c670c2d38",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/355b58689c55ca969ce195edd651967c670c2d38",
      "message": "Build only the watcher's production chain in its image\n\nWith every manifest present, `--filter midgard-watcher...` also selected the\ndev-only midgard-node chain, whose sources the image does not copy.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T08:39:07Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "8eeda7e5f1eed8993a7318c549b50e21a8000dc6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/8eeda7e5f1eed8993a7318c549b50e21a8000dc6",
      "message": "Build every runtime dependency in the node image and copy all manifests\n\nThe node image relied on a midgard-node prebuild that 0c1adbd33 removed, so\nit shipped without lucid-midgard, core or sdk dist and the smoke run could not\nload the sdk. The watcher image's deploy resolves its midgard-node workspace\nedge, so it needs every workspace manifest, as the node image already has.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T08:30:26Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "8f8b391f88c73385d317c9d69e45e230c1828ee8",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/8f8b391f88c73385d317c9d69e45e230c1828ee8",
      "message": "Give both images the test-support manifest and the Go test fixture\n\nEvery package lists @al-ft/midgard-test-support as a dev dependency, so the\nfrozen install and `pnpm deploy` need its manifest in the image. The\nwatcher's Go tests read tests/support/conway-block.hex from outside the\nnative-chain-sync directory, which the build stage never copied.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T06:59:58Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6705ce632bfd5505f628aa5edacfd5c1e9cc3285",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6705ce632bfd5505f628aa5edacfd5c1e9cc3285",
      "message": "Fix the first CI run: script modes, the vendored uplc tarball, the MPF prebuild\n\n- build-aiken-fork.sh and start-test-postgres.sh were committed as 100644\n  (core.fileMode=false hides it), so the fork build exited 126. A test now\n  reads the index modes of every script a workflow runs by path and of every\n  hook.\n- demo/.dockerignore dropped every .tgz, and neither image copied vendor/,\n  so pnpm could not resolve the vendored uplc override in either image.\n- The throughput gates import lucid-midgard's dist; their job now builds it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T05:52:56Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ee8429f0a3cb941cebcad07053a8e4600fc00295",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ee8429f0a3cb941cebcad07053a8e4600fc00295",
      "message": "Merge the Wave 1 CI hardening into the agent-hardening branch\n\nIntegration on top of the merge:\n- Repo Tools CI also runs the generated required-checks check and the three\n  agent-documentation checks, so the rules they guard carry [ci: ...] tags.\n- Preflight drops its pending-sibling list now that the workflow lint and\n  trigger test have landed; the registry test requires every script to exist.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T05:44:37Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ef6cc3cad13b03491912b0450bc641eb6a4c0046",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ef6cc3cad13b03491912b0450bc641eb6a4c0046",
      "message": "Record Wave 1 CI progress in the hardening plan\n\nTick W1.2 to W1.7 and W2.14 with where each landed, and record the local\nrun of the split Node CI under W1.1, which stays open: the remaining reds\ncome from the selected deployment profile, not from CI.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T05:38:27Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "cb3961d73ccd8b6d719843c3ed0616abfe59b824",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/cb3961d73ccd8b6d719843c3ed0616abfe59b824",
      "message": "Format the three files the workspace format check rejects\n\npnpm --dir demo format-check failed at 71e605e46 on three files from that\ncheckpoint. This is prettier --write output only.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T05:06:43Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "2d9ee1b3630624a050ce63d503050f90d994dacb",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/2d9ee1b3630624a050ce63d503050f90d994dacb",
      "message": "Sort imports and exports that demo lint rejects",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:58:32Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "349a7bea4c30c16b13bd252561a937be79b163c7",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/349a7bea4c30c16b13bd252561a937be79b163c7",
      "message": "Let ESLint type-check the fault-proofs Vitest config\n\nThe config sits outside the package tsconfig and was missing from the\ndefault-project list, so demo lint failed to parse it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:54:31Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "39180b9887a17b25c5326d71d8cfc268325934e5",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/39180b9887a17b25c5326d71d8cfc268325934e5",
      "message": "Point the verification guide at preflight instead of a hand-kept table\n\nThe required-checks table in verification.md is replaced by preflight and the\nlist it generates. Preflight gains the agent-config check and the e2e runbook\nvalidator; the five rows it cannot run yet stay in a short hand-kept table.\nRules that a hook, the doctor or the runbook validator now enforce carry that\ntag instead of [review].",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:51:15Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "e07088d64aab3d5d58885e8c6e8121b2552f441d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/e07088d64aab3d5d58885e8c6e8121b2552f441d",
      "message": "Wire the landed agent-doc checks into preflight and exempt its generated list\n\nThe enforcement-tag checker now skips docs/agents/required-checks.md: it is\ngenerated from the preflight registry, which is itself the enforcement, so\nits rules need no tags and its length no budget. The misses log is marked as\na future path for the doc-link check, and preflight no longer treats the\nagent-doc scripts as pending siblings.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:49:18Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "12da39f8581a2aa54ebdeb8986a2abd523d3e848",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/12da39f8581a2aa54ebdeb8986a2abd523d3e848",
      "message": "Merge enforcement-tagged rules, doc checks and per-worktree isolation\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tdocs/exec-plans/agent-contribution-hardening.md",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:46:30Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "00677c22fb248e73a5f894d76fc1addde709f893",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/00677c22fb248e73a5f894d76fc1addde709f893",
      "message": "Record Wave 2 rule and worktree progress in the hardening plan\n\nTicks the Wave 2 items that are now in the tree and notes what remains\nof the partial ones: the operator compose files still fix their ports,\nthe event-history artifacts still sit in the tree, the core dist\nassertion waits for the preflight, and fast-check is kept for W6.3.\nThe plan's citations of another repository's files and of future\ndeliverables carry doc-links markers.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:45:34Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "48d059ad9cc6e0480b2865f9a14d4232dcabc818",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/48d059ad9cc6e0480b2865f9a14d4232dcabc818",
      "message": "Keep CLAUDE.md a pointer and shared agent settings narrow\n\nCLAUDE.md is loaded by one agent and AGENTS.md by the rest, so a rule\nwritten only in CLAUDE.md is a second source that drifts. The lint\nrequires every tracked CLAUDE.md to be a symlink to AGENTS.md or a short\npage that links it, states no rule, carries no enforcement tag, and\npoints each paragraph at a tracked path.\n\nA tracked .claude/settings.json applies to everyone who opens the\nrepository. The lint allows only a schema, SessionStart hooks that run\none tracked script without shell composition, deny and ask permission\nlists, and includeCoAuthoredBy false; allow lists, defaultMode,\nadditionalDirectories, env and every other key fail, as does a tracked\nsettings.local.json. No settings file is tracked today; the fixture\ntests show each widening is caught.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-26T04:45:28Z"
    }
  ],
